ld-time music», el yodel de Jimmie Rodgers, el crooning de Bing Crosby, el boogie-woogie, el jump blues de Louis Jordan (nacimiento de facto del rhythm'n'blues), la guitarra jazzística de T-Bone Walker, Woody Guthrie como primer gran cantautor y la exótica de Les Baxter. En paralelo, la vanguardia clásica (Russolo, Satie, Varèse, Cage, Schaeffer) anticipa el ruido, el ambient y la electrónica.","color":"#f59e0b","family":"Raíces: rock'n'roll, country y roots","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#antecedentes"},{"id":231270189174368,"name":"Easy listening / Space age pop","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1954,"end":1968,"desc":"El primer lounge quiso explorar el nuevo espacio —exterior y sonoro—: estéreo, ondiolín y theremín al servicio de una música cómoda y misteriosa.","color":"#f472b6","family":"Rock, synth-pop y canción","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#space-age"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":115019818650237,"artist":"Les Baxter","artist_id":62808103140795,"title":"Music Out of the Moon","year":1950,"ess":0,"yt":"KW0t23AdNXw","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Antecedentes (1892-1950)","scene_id":73745448294291,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#antecedentes","chapters":["Sección 2.1"],"pages":[[1,9,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":9,"text":"…that, indirectly, publicized exotic sounds. Then (1948) Rodgers & Hammerstein's Tale Of The South Pacific became a Broadway hit. Finally (1950) Les Baxter's Music Out of the Moon incorporated exotic themes in instrumental easy-listening music. The end of the decade and the beginning of the 1950s were…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":202,"text":"…and eastern instruments, and others to further expand their music towards other ethnic sounds. It was an evolution of the Byrds' raga-rock and of Les Baxter's and Martin Denny's \"exotica\", but facilitated by a larger availability of exotic instruments and of exotic recordings. The naive multi-cultural…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":310,"text":"…and blues\" records ？ Aristocrat changes its name to Chess ？ Jac Holzman founds Elektra in New York to promote new folk and jazz musicians 1950 ？ Les Baxter's Music Out of the Moon incorporates exotic themes in instrumental music ？ Dutch electronics giant Philips enters the recording business ？ The white…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Pioneer and Master of Space Age Pop and Exotica","body":"Les Baxter debutó con el álbum \"Music Out of the Moon\" y se convirtió en el pionero y maestro del Space Age Pop. También experimentó con gran éxito en el género Exotica. \"Les Baxter, quien debutó con este álbum, se convertió en el pionero y maestro del género, y también provó con mucho acierto con la exótica.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"Así sonaba el pop de la era atómica","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LqPX20XSa_s"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Sampled in Intergalactic","body":"An electronic album released in 1968 by Les Baxter was sampled in the Beastie Boys' song \"Intergalactic,\" specifically appearing just after the one-minute mark. \"This electronic album from 1968 is by Les Baxter, and it's in the song starting just after the one-minute mark.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Remembering the Beastie Boys Part 2","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_BTe15NooI"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"star on Hollywood Walk of Fame","body":"Won.","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q17985761"}]}],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","tit